n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3b-c)\\times (9a-2b) & = \\\\ ((3b)\\times (9a))-((3b)\\times (2b))-(c\\times (9a))+(c\\times (2b))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3b-c)\\times (9a-2b) & = \\\\ ((3b)\\times (9a))-((3b)\\times (2b))-(c\\times (9a))+(c\\times (2b)) & = \\\\ (3\\cdot 9)(b\\times a)-(3\\cdot 2)(b\\times b)-9(c\\times a)+2(c\\times b) & = \\\\ 27(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b)-9(c\\times a)+2(c\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $b\\times b=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b)-9(c\\times a)+2(c\\times b) & = \\\\ -27(a\\times b)-6(0)+9(a\\times c)+2(c\\times b) & = \\\\ -27(a\\times b)+9(a\\times c)+2(c\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-27(a\\times b)+9(a\\times c)+2(c\\times b) & = \\\\ -27⟨0,0,1⟩+9⟨0,-1,3⟩+2⟨0,2,0⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨0,0,-27⟩+⟨0,-9,27⟩+⟨0,4,0⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨0,-5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370263 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370264 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370265 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370266 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370267 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1041 "selection" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370263 13194139535852 true] [17592186370262 1110 #uuid "370c8336-471e-5ee0-978e-6983bfe78b67" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370263 1034 "⟨0,-5,0⟩" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535852 true] [17592186370263 1111 #uuid "56e53634-9539-5a98-9e07-16fefaf84621" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370264 10