a724d4bf" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370349 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370349 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535852 true] [17592186370349 1111 #uuid "9fc59cb3-cdb5-560b-9621-68e5ee5291f3" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370350 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370351 13194139535852 true] [17592186370350 1089 "q-75825" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370350 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535852 true] [17592186370350 1100 "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370350 1113 #uuid "2eba1a60-af4c-5293-b4c6-5aa086d9d5e4" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370350 1145 "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-8=(x+2)(x-4).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8} & =\\frac{3x-6}{(x+2)(x-4)}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n3x-6=A(x-4)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(4)-6 & =A(4-4)+B(4+2) \\\\ 6 & =6B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-2)-6 & =A(-2-4)+B(-2+2) \\\\ -12 & =-6A \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}=\\frac{2}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}(x-4)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}(x-4)|{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370352 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370353 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370354 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370355 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370356 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1041 "selection" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370355 13194139535852 true] [17592186370351 1110 #uuid "c59e863d-947d-5701-b687-a25fe7f0fee9" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370352 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535852 true] [17592186370352 1111 #uuid "8af61602-e5f1-50b0-b7fb-da21cf2dc2dd" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370353 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535852 true] [17592186370353 1111 #uuid "549f9742-aeb3-5082-9612-6ec6bd2c2e26" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370354 1034 "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535852 true] [17592186370354 1111 #uuid "fd993e3f-4d58-5847-a76d-6919cbadf320" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370355 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" 13194139535852 true] [17592186370355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535852 true] [17592186370355 1111 #uuid "a11e5dfd-52e6-5b6d-9f2a-820bc2d1db43" 1